Temperature
Body temperature may be recorded in the mouth, 
axilla, ear or rectum. A ''normal'' mouth temperature 
is 35.8-37°C. Those in the ear and rectum are 0.5°C 
higher and in the axilla 0.5°C lower. There is a diurnal 
