Pinard stethoscope (Fig. 5.13) or now more often 
with a handheld Doppler device.
Vaginal examination in pregnancy
Vaginal examination (VE) is not usually recommended 
in early pregnancy. If there is bleeding or retention 
of urine, it may provide useful information, but the 
widespread availability of ultrasound scanning has 
made diagnosis in this situation far less intrusive. In 
