The mother faces the baby to one side and holds him firmly, with 
one arm around the head and the other around the upper arm and 
shoulder. 
Figure 6.5  How to hold a baby to allow the mouth and throat 
to be examined. The baby faces the examiner, with the mother 
holding him firmly with one hand on the forehead and the other 
holding both arms.', 3903),
