Ventricular tachycardia
Ventricular tachycardia is defined as three or more 
consecutive ventricular beats at a rate above 120 per 
minute. Ventricular depolarization inevitably occurs 
slowly by abnormal pathways, producing a broad 
QRS complex. This distinguishes it from most atrial 
