The pulmonary artery wedge pressure is obtained 
during right-heart catheterization by advancing the 
catheter distally into the pulmonary arterial tree until 
the tip wedges in a small branch. Alternatively, a 
catheter with a preterminal balloon (Swan-Ganz 
