Typical patient
■ Either middle-aged or elderly patient with malignant 
disease (usually breast or lung) or patients of any age 
with tuberculosis
Major symptoms
■ Dyspnoea and variable circulatory collapse
Major signs
■ Low-output state (hypotension, oliguria, cold periphery), 
