Serology
If a recent streptococcal throat infection can be 
confirmed by demonstrating an elevated serum 
antistreptolysin O titre, Jones''s criteria may be used 
for the diagnosis of rheumatic fever (Box 13.26). 
The presence of two major criteria, or one major and 
two minor criteria, indicates a high probability of 
rheumatic fever. In suspected viral pericarditis or 
myocarditis, the aetiological diagnosis depends on 
the demonstration of elevated viral antibody titres 
in acute serum samples, which decline during convalescence. Virus may sometimes be cultured from 
throat swabs and stools.
