All UK hospital inpatients are now assessed for 
their risk of malnutrition. The most common assessment method used by healthcare staff is the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST). This involves 
calculating the patient''s BMI and then adding on a 
score for the percentage of unexpected weight loss 
and a score for the degree of acute illness. The final 
score is used to trigger a full dietary assessment and 
initiation of treatment in those who need it. Patients 
should be screened weekly whilst in hospital and at 
every outpatient attendance.
