Visible pulsation of the abdominal aorta may be 
noticed in the epigastrium and is a frequent finding 
in nervous, thin patients. It must be distinguished 
from an aneurysm of the abdominal aorta, where 
pulsation is more obvious and a widened aorta is felt 
on palpation.
