Fractures
X-rays are often the first investigation in suspected 
fractures and in joint disease. In traumatic fractures, 
X-rays are diagnostic and are used to check alignment 
of the fracture and healing. X-rays of a fracture are 
also important in excluding pathological fracture 
associated with metabolic bone disease, a focal benign 
