matrix has solidified and is studded with red or white 
blood cells. Granular casts probably represent degenerate cellular casts and have a grainy appearance. Hyaline 
casts contain no elements or debris and may be seen 
in small numbers in normal urine. It is usual to express 
the number of cells or casts seen per high-power 
field. The presence of red cell casts should alert one 
