Examining the fundi
Look carefully at the optic disc/cup, the retinal vessels 
and the retina and macula (Fig. 20.9).
Optic disc
This marks the point where the retinal axons exit 
the back of the eye to form the optic nerve. It corresponds to the physiological blind spot. The normal 
disc is round or slightly oval. If there is astigmatism, 
the disc may appear more oval than normal. There 
