abnormally pale disc is a sign of optic atrophy 
(Fig. 20.10). In addition, in optic atrophy there 
is a reduction in the number of capillaries 
crossing the edge of the disc, from the normal 
10 to 7 or fewer (Kestenbaum''s sign). The 
